## Dataset

* Dataset is cleanned and removed the dublicates. No need to run the 02_Dataset_Cleanning.ipynb and 03_Dataset_Cleaning.ipynb 
  because the splitting is done(70% train,15% val,15% test) but do the 01_count_images_ipynb(for you understanding and viva purpose).
* * This project uses a custom-prepared rice leaf disease dataset containing seven classes:                                                                                            
* Bacterial Leaf Blight
* Brown Spot
* Healthy
* Leaf Blast
* Leaf Scald
* Leaf Smut
* Narrow Brown Spot

The complete dataset is approximately **305 MB** and is hosted separately on Google Drive due to its size.

**Dataset Download:**
[Download the Custom Rice Leaf Disease Dataset](https://drive.google.com/file/d/18BHV1D9tbTUILVgqLqLU7FfbN391Hk7H/view?usp=sharing)

### Dataset Path

After downloading and extracting the dataset, organize it as follows:

```text
Processed_RiceDisease_Dataset/
├── train/
│   ├── bacterial_leaf_blight/
│   ├── brown_spot/
│   ├── healthy/
│   ├── leaf_blast/
│   ├── leaf_scald/
│   ├── leaf_smut/
│   └── narrow_brown_spot/
│
├── val/
│   ├── bacterial_leaf_blight/
│   ├── brown_spot/
│   ├── healthy/
│   ├── leaf_blast/
│   ├── leaf_scald/
│   ├── leaf_smut/
│   └── narrow_brown_spot/
│
└── test/
    ├── bacterial_leaf_blight/
    ├── brown_spot/
    ├── healthy/
    ├── leaf_blast/
    ├── leaf_scald/
    ├── leaf_smut/
    └── narrow_brown_spot/
```

Set the dataset path in the code according to your local system.

Example:

```python
DATASET_PATH = r"C:\path\to\Processed_RiceDisease_Dataset"
```

## Model Performance

The performance of the implemented models is compared below:

| Model                                       |     Accuracy |
| ------------------------------------------- | -----------: |
| **CNN**                                     |   **82.00%** |
| **ResNet50**                                |   **95.00%** |
| **DenseNet121**                             |   **89.00%** |
| **EfficientNetB3**                          |   **92.00%** |
| **YOLOv11**                                 |   **97.00%** |
| **CNN + DenseNet121**                       |   **89.32%** |
| **EfficientNetB3 + ResNet50**               |   **93.00%** |
| **ResNet50 + YOLOv11**                      |   **65.00%** |
| **EfficientNetB3 + DenseNet121 (Proposed)** | **97.26% ⭐** |

The proposed **EfficientNetB3 + DenseNet121 hybrid feature fusion model** achieved **97.26% accuracy**, demonstrating strong performance for multi-class rice leaf disease classification.
